### FILE README.md exec=0 bytes=716 encoding=utf-8
# quiet-otter

a test project

## Checks

Run these before opening a PR. CI runs the same ones.

```sh
docker build -t quiet-otter . && docker compose up -d app   # data volume: appdata:/data
gofmt -l . && go vet ./... && go test ./...
```

The owner (`someone`) may push their own work directly to `main` without a PR or passing CI. CI still runs after a push; releases retain their CI gates. Force-push, deletion, and merge commits remain blocked for everyone.

Other accounts must use a squash PR with passing, up-to-date `ci`. Agents must use PRs and CI even when authenticated as the owner (see `AGENTS.md`). GitHub checks the pushing account, so enforcing a human/agent boundary requires separate credentials.

### END
### FILE SECURITY.md exec=0 bytes=213 encoding=utf-8
# Security Policy

Please report vulnerabilities privately via
**Security → Report a vulnerability** on this repository (GitHub private vulnerability reporting).
Do not open public issues for security problems.

### END
